[Level "4"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined: Capablanca Variation, Anti-Cambridge Springs Variation"]
[Why "The game that decided the title: a textbook on converting an outside passed pawn in a rook ending. After winning a pawn in the middlegame (24.Qxa7; engine says White's edge was still only +0.2, so Capablanca's later moves mattered), Alekhine reaches rook and four pawns against rook and three with a passed a-pawn, puts the rook behind it (54.Ra4!, +2.9), ties Black's rook to a6, and walks his king across the board (62.Kd4, 64.Kf4, 65.Kg5) to attack the kingside pawns while Black's rook is passive. Rooks belong behind passed pawns, and the active king wins what the pawn alone cannot."]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Nbd7 5. e3 c6 6. a3 Be7 7. Nf3 O-O 8. Bd3 dxc4 9. Bxc4 Nd5 10. Bxe7 Qxe7 11. Ne4 N5f6 12. Ng3 c5 13. O-O Nb6 14. Ba2 cxd4 15. Nxd4 g6 16. Rc1 Bd7 17. Qe2 Rac8 18. e4 e5 19. Nf3 Kg7 20. h3 h6 21. Qd2 Be6 22. Bxe6 Qxe6 23. Qa5 { Key: White nets the a-pawn; the queenside majority becomes a passed a-pawn. } 23... Nc4 24. Qxa7 Nxb2 25. Rxc8 Rxc8 26. Qxb7 Nc4 27. Qb4 Ra8 28. Ra1 Qc6 29. a4 { Key: Simplification into queen and rook each, with the extra a-pawn. } 29... Nxe4 30. Nxe5 Qd6 31. Qxc4 Qxe5 32. Re1 Nd6 33. Qc1 Qf6 34. Ne4 Nxe4 35. Rxe4 Rb8 36. Re2 Ra8 37. Ra2 Ra5 38. Qc7 Qa6 39. Qc3+ Kh7 40. Rd2 Qb6 41. Rd7 Qb1+ 42. Kh2 Qb8+ 43. g3 Rf5 44. Qd4 Qe8 45. Rd5 Rf3 46. h4 Qh8 47. Qb6 Qa1 48. Kg2 Rf6 49. Qd4 { Key: The rook behind the passed pawn; Black's rook becomes a spectator. } 49... Qxd4 50. Rxd4 Kg7 51. a5 Ra6 52. Rd5 Rf6 53. Rd4 Ra6 54. Ra4 Kf6 55. Kf3 { Key: A waiting move forces Black's king to give way. } 55... Ke5 56. Ke3 h5 57. Kd3 Kd5 58. Kc3 Kc5 59. Ra2 Kb5 60. Kb3 Kc5 61. Kc3 Kb5 62. Kd4 Rd6+ 63. Ke5 Re6+ 64. Kf4 { Key: The king attacks the pawns while the rook holds the a-pawn; the rook trade leaves a won pawn ending (engine +6.0). 82.Re7 and Capablanca resigned. } 64... Ka6 65. Kg5 Re5+ 66. Kh6 Rf5 67. f4 Rc5 68. Ra3 Rc7 69. Kg7 Rd7 70. f5 gxf5 71. Kh6 f4 72. gxf4 Rd5 73. Kg7 Rf5 74. Ra4 Kb5 75. Re4 Ka6 76. Kh6 Rxa5 77. Re5 Ra1 78. Kxh5 Rg1 79. Rg5 Rh1 80. Rf5 Kb6 81. Rxf7 Kc6 82. Re7 1-0

