[Level "3"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined: Exchange Variation, Reshevsky Variation"]
[Why "The clean textbook minority attack in the Carlsbad structure: 11.Rab1, 12.b4, 13.b5 and 14.bxc6 leave Black with a weak pawn on c6 (engine +0.9 from a level opening), which Smyslov then wins through the b-file (22.Rb7, 26.Rb5) while Keres's kingside counterplay (...h5-h4) is too slow; the game ends as a technical win against the isolated d-pawn. Two pawns attack three to create one weakness; keep pieces aimed at c6 and the b-file open."]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 c6 5. e3 Nbd7 6. cxd5 { Key: The Carlsbad structure: a2 b2 d4 e3 against a7 b7 c6 d5. } 6... exd5 7. Bd3 Be7 8. Nf3 O-O 9. Qc2 Re8 10. O-O Nf8 11. Rab1 { Key: The minority attack in four moves; c6 is now a backward pawn on an open file. } 11... Ng6 12. b4 Bd6 13. b5 Bd7 14. bxc6 Bxc6 15. Qb3 { Key: The rook reaches the seventh; c6 and a7 are both weak. } 15... Be7 16. Bxf6 Bxf6 17. Bb5 Qd6 18. Rfc1 h5 19. Ne2 h4 20. Bxc6 bxc6 21. Qa4 Ne7 22. Rb7 a5 23. h3 Reb8 24. Rcb1 Rxb7 25. Rxb7 { Key: Black gives the c-pawn for activity; the h-pawn falls as well. } 25... c5 26. Rb5 cxd4 27. Nexd4 Rc8 28. Nb3 Bc3 29. Qxh4 Rc4 30. g4 a4 31. Nbd4 { Key: Two pawns up with the a-pawn running (engine +5.0). Keres resigned. } 31... Bxd4 32. Nxd4 Qe5 33. Nf3 Qd6 34. Ra5 Rc8 35. Rxa4 Ng6 36. Qh5 Qf6 37. Qf5 Qc6 38. Ra7 Rf8 39. Rd7 d4 40. Rxd4 Ra8 41. a4 1-0

